{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1462519-sheets-for-the-visually-impaired","id":1462519,"title":"Sheets for the Visually Impaired","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-02T23:26:12-07:00","id":1462519,"title":"Sheets for the Visually Impaired","content":"I am running Promethean in particular, though I often run other CofD games and hope there is an option for all of them.<br /> <br /> I have a player who is visually impaired. The Roll20 sheets, including the community-managed updated versions, are not readable to a screen reader. Everything is treated as a button and isn't labeled so the reader can't read them out.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know of any other sheet management websites or character generator programs we could use instead?<br /> <br /> At the moment, I am probably going to have to have her use MrGone's sheet and upload it to a shared Drive folder between sessions, but this is a bit clunky.<br /> <br /> Other options very welcome.<br /> <br /> Edit: I should specify, if it was not clear, that this is for an online game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T09:42:23-07:00","id":1462660,"title":"","content":"Don't know anything already made.<br /> <br /> Personally I use Hero Lab for D&amp;D and M&amp;M and is a fantastic tool, but their official CoD release is actually just the first edition core blue book, still called World of Darkness. It does have a powerful system to write your own system, though, so making it work with up-to-date CoD is perfectly doable, but no small feat. It does have a very useful wiki and helpful community in their forums, but this would be still a reasonable amount of editing and programming.<br /> <br /> It is easy enough that for anyone wanting also to warm up programming skills or an easy learning environment, I would recommend anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}